A Writer PDF carries no comment annotations unless the caller asks for them.

pdfexport.cxx defaults bExportNotes to true, so every comment of a Writer document became a /Text annotation in the
PDF. Stock LibreOffice 25.8.7.3 headless writes none (the PDF dialog's configuration default is false), and the
owner decided on 2026-10-25 (BUG-36, spreadsheet comments) that comments are off by default with an advanced option
to turn them on, extended to Writer on 2026-10-29. Under __EMSCRIPTEN__ the default is now false. An explicit
ExportNotes=true in the filter data, which is how the future Advanced option would arrive, is read by the property
loop below the default and still wins. Editable outputs are not affected: DOCX and ODT keep their comments.

Module-scoped (-documents): the documents module is the Writer module, and it is rebuilt for BUG-48 anyway; the
bridge is not changed because engine/bridge/ is part of every module's fingerprint.

diff --git a/filter/source/pdf/pdfexport.cxx b/filter/source/pdf/pdfexport.cxx
--- a/filter/source/pdf/pdfexport.cxx
+++ b/filter/source/pdf/pdfexport.cxx
@@ -406,7 +406,15 @@
             bool bUseTaggedPDF = false;
             sal_Int32 nPDFTypeSelection = 0;
             bool bPDFUACompliance = false;
+#ifdef __EMSCRIPTEN__
+            // A PDF carries no comment annotations unless the caller asks for them (owner decision: BUG-36 for
+            // spreadsheets, extended to Writer 2026-10-29, matching stock LibreOffice headless). An explicit
+            // FilterData ExportNotes=true, the future Advanced "include comments" option, still wins: the
+            // property loop below assigns it over this default.
+            bool bExportNotes = false;
+#else
             bool bExportNotes = true;
+#endif
             bool bExportNotesInMargin = false;
             bool bExportNotesPages = false;
             bool bExportOnlyNotesPages = false;
